This product builds on matter.js (https://github.com/matter-js/matter.js, Apache-2.0) and
MQTT.js (https://github.com/mqttjs/MQTT.js, MIT) as dependencies; it contains no copied code
from either, nor from matterbridge or its plugins.

The test fixtures test/fixtures/z2m/bridge-devices.json and bridge-groups.json are copied
unchanged from matterbridge-zigbee2mqtt (https://github.com/Luligu/matterbridge-zigbee2mqtt,
src/mock/, commit c72dd312d0899e930aec220e67b8959f10221eb0), Copyright 2023-2025 Luca Liguori,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. They are used as a test corpus only.

The Home Assistant MQTT discovery test corpus in test/fixtures/ha/ is documented in
test/fixtures/ha/README.md: captures of the maintainer's own devices (ESPHome, zigbee2mqtt's own
discovery, his MQTT adapters), anonymised, and payloads written by hand in the shape the documentation
of Tasmota, Shelly, Z-Wave JS UI and OpenMQTTGateway describes; nothing is copied from those projects.
The abbreviation tables in src/importers/ha/types.ts list the key names of Home Assistant's MQTT
integration (https://github.com/home-assistant/core, Apache-2.0), which are the protocol, not code.
